    {
      "id": "3b2271ed-d9bc-47ba-80d4-5a6e88e60514",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        912,
        -624
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 700,
        "height": 1201,
        "content": "# Weekly podcast analytics with week-on-week scoring and AI insights\n\nThe Spotify for Creators dashboard shows one episode at a time and keeps no history. This pulls every episode each Monday, keeps one row per episode in a sheet, works out what moved since last week, scores each episode against your own averages, and emails a digest saying what is working and what to make next.\n\n### How it works\n1. A weekly schedule runs, then one cheap call checks the token first. It expires after hours, so if it died you get an email and the run stops without touching last week's data.\n2. Every episode is fetched with a second between calls. One with no data yet returns empty rather than failing the run.\n3. Last week's rows are read back and compared with today's, giving a plays change and a growing, flat or new status.\n4. Each episode is scored on reach and retention against your own averages, then ranked top performer, average or underperforming.\n5. Rows are matched on Episode ID, so an episode already in the sheet is updated in place, not added again.\n6. A ranked briefing goes to GPT, which finds patterns across titles, length and retention and returns what is working, what to fix and three episode ideas.\n7. The digest email arrives with top and bottom tables and that advice.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add your OpenAI key and connect Google Sheets and Gmail.\n2. Log into Spotify for Creators, open the network tab, copy your podcast ID and Authorization header.\n3. Paste both into Set config with your sheet ID, email and podcast name.\n4. Create a tab called Episode Analytics with a header row including Episode ID.\n\n### Customization\nChange the score weighting if plays matter more than retention."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
